\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Laws in the Aftermath of the Court Decision\b0\par\par\uc2 1,494 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 17\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 on in 1997. New Hampshire \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will most likely stay accessible, though it is not expressly protected by state law. State courts have not determined whether New Mexico's Constitution protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. New Mexico State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Rhode Island STATE PARTY CONTROL STATE PARTY CONTROL STATE PARTY CONTROL STATE PARTY CONTROL State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Colorado The state's high court has recognized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections under its Constitution, and state law protects the procedure. Illinois The state's high court has recognized the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its Constitution. Recently enacted laws protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and expand access. Massachusetts The state's high court has recognized the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its Constitution. Minnesota State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and lawmakers have introduced bills to make the state a ''sanctuary'' for those seeking the procedure. California State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  A new law expands access to providers and shields both providers and patients from out-of-state lawsuits. Connecticut State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a new law expands access to providers. Delaware State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a new law expands access to providers. Hawaii State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and new laws increase access to providers and insurance coverage. Maryland State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy, and the governor has proposed making the state a ''sanctuary'' for those seeking the procedure. New Jersey State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Legislators have proposed other protections, including an amendment to the State Constitution. New York State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy, and the Legislature approved $15 million to support those seeking the procedure. Oregon State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy. In November, voters will decide if the State Constitution should include \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection. Vermont State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and recent laws expand access to providers. Washington State law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Maine These states are expected to maintain the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and many are working to expand access to the procedure by requiring insurance to pay for it and increasing the number of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Legal Without Roe Legal and Expanded Without Roe The state's high court has recognized a right to ''reproductive choice'' under its Constitution. Alaska Gov. Sen. House Note: In Alaska, control of the state's House of Representatives is split between parties. Local law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy. The city plans to bolster protections, though Congress ultimately oversees the city's laws. Washington, D.C. Note: Washington, D.C., has a mayor and a unicameral district council. Gov. Sen. House Restrictions Are Uncertain Lawmakers in these states have signaled some interest in restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In some, the governor or a state constitutional amendment may protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the short term. In others, pre-Roe laws that prohibited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the 1973 decision could be enforced again. STATE PARTY CONTROL The governor may call a special session of the state legislature to consider new laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A majority of lawmakers signed a letter in March asking him to do so if Roe were overturned. Indiana In June, the state's high court overruled a 2018 decision that said the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was protected under the State Constitution. The state previously enacted a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, which was permanently blocked by a judge, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are likely to seek its enforcement. Iowa The state's high court ruled that a pregnant woman's right to personal autonomy is protected in its Constitution. Kansans will decide in August whether its Constitution should be amended to say it contains no right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Kansas The state has a law from before Roe that would ban nearly all abortions, but it has been blocked in state court. The Democratic governor and attorney general have also said they will not enforce the ban. Michigan The state has a ban after 20 weeks of pregnancy, which is not in effect, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are likely to seek its enforcement. The state's high court ruled that its Constitution protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Montana The state has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban enacted before Roe, but it was modified in 1973 to bar the procedure after 20 weeks of pregnancy. The 20-week ban is not in effect, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents may seek its enforcement. North Carolina \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not protected by state law. Republicans currently control the state legislature, but the current Democratic governor has vetoed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Pennsylvania \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will most likely stay accessible, though it is not expressly protected by state law. Split control of the state legislature may prevent significant changes until the next election in 2023. Virginia A bill to enact a trigger ban failed in the Legislature this year. The governor is expected to call a special session to pass a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nebraska Note: Nebraska has a unicameral Legislature that is nonpartisan. The state has a law from before Roe that bans nearly all abortions and makes performing them a felony. The Democratic governor and attorney general have said they will not enforce the ban. Wisconsin Now These states have trigger laws that have already or will soon ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the Supreme Court's decision; have moved in recent months to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of the court's decision; or have existing bans that were temporarily blocked by a judge but could now be enforced. Where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already prohibited or is likely to be restricted STATE PARTY CONTROL WHEN IN EFFECT STATE PARTY CONTROL STATE PARTY CONTROL WHEN IN EFFECT Prohibited Without Roe The state has a law from before Roe that bans nearly all abortions. A judge blocked a more recent total ban on the procedure, with no exceptions for rape or incest, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are likely to seek its enforcement now that Roe has been overturned. Now Gov. Sen. House Gov. Sen. House Alabama \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned with no exceptions for rape or incest. Arkansas Now A trigger law banning nearly all abortions takes effect 30 days after the Supreme Court's decision. Idaho Soon \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned with no exceptions for rape or incest. Kentucky Now \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned with no exceptions for rape or incest. Louisiana Now A trigger law banning nearly all abortions takes effect within days. A 15-week ban is now in effect. Mississippi Soon \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned with no exceptions for rape or incest. Missouri Now A trigger law banning nearly all abortions takes effect 30 days after the Supreme Court's decision. North Dakota Soon The state prohibited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the point of fertilization in May, with exceptions for rape and incest. The law relies on civilian enforcement. Oklahoma Now \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned with no exceptions for rape or incest. South Dakota Now A trigger law banning nearly all abortions, with no exceptions for rape or incest, takes effect 30 days from the court decision. A six-week ban is currently in effect. Texas Soon Voters approved an amendment to the state's Constitution that denies any right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Lawmakers may use the amendment to enact a total ban. West Virginia Soon A trigger law banning nearly all abortions takes effect within days of the Supreme Court's decision. Wyoming Soon The state enacted an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after 15 weeks of pregnancy, which will go into effect on July 1. The state's high court recognized the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its Constitution three decades ago, but the court has become more conservative, with three of the seven judges appointed by the Republican governor. Florida The state enacted a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, but a court blocked it. The state filed an appeal and a court stayed the case pending the Supreme Court's decision on Dobbs. Georgia \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned after six weeks of pregnancy, after a judge allowed an older law to go into effect. Ohio The state enacted a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, but a court blocked it. The state filed an appeal and a court stayed the case pending the Supreme Court's decision on Dobbs. South Carolina The state enacted an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after 15 weeks, with no exceptions for rape or incest, which takes effect in September. Arizona has an inactive ban from before 1973, but the governor has said the 15-week ban will take precedence. Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned with exceptions for rape, incest and to save the life of the woman. Utah Now Restricted Without Roe A trigger law banning nearly all abortions, with no exceptions for rape or incest, takes effect 30 days from the Supreme Court's decision. The state attorney general has filed an emergency motion to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tennessee immediately. Tennessee Soon \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Laws in the Aftermath of the Court Decision By Allison McCann, Amy Schoenfeld Walker, Taylor Johnston and Larry Buchanan. Additional reporting by Margot Sanger-Katz and Ava Sasani.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220625ei6p0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
