\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 The Global View: Most Countries Are Increasing Protections\b0\par\par\uc2 By Adam Liptak \par \uc2 352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Around the world, many governments have been moving toward easier access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with more than 50 countries liberalizing their laws in the past three decades. By contrast, a recent Supreme Court brief filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers said that overruling Roe puts the U.S. ''in the company of countries like Poland and Nicaragua as one of only a few countries moving toward greater restrictions on legal access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past 20 years.'' Opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  point to different statistics. In a legislative finding justifying the Mississippi law at issue in Friday's ruling, its drafters said that the American approach, which required states to allow abortions until about 23 weeks of pregnancy, was an outlier. ''The United States is one of only seven nations in the world that permits nontherapeutic or elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ondemand after the 20th week of gestation,'' the finding said.\par \par \uc2  ''In fact, fully 75 percent of all nations do not permit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 weeks' gestation, except (in most instances) to save the life and to preserve the physical health of the mother.'' Twelve weeks is a common nominal limit in other nations, legal experts said, though the social context is usually quite different. There are generally few obstacles to obtaining abortions abroad, and public insurance is commonplace. In a Supreme Court brief, Mississippi officials focused on the nation's adversaries. ''The United States finds itself in the company of China and North Korea as some of the only countries that permit elective abortions after 20 weeks' gestation,'' the brief said. Lawyers for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers challenging the Mississippi law said that the nation's closest peers have adopted limits similar to those in Roe. ''In countries with legal traditions and democratic values most comparable to the United States, such as Great Britain and Canada, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal until at least viability,'' they wrote. ''And many countries that have limits earlier in pregnancy continue to permit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for broad social and health reasons after that point, functionally allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in pregnancy.''\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220625ei6p0004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
