\par\par \uc2 Movies, Performing Arts/Weekend Desk; SECTC\par \b \uc2 The Janes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Beatrice Loayza \par \uc2 379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 7\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 This HBO documentary spotlights the women activists who banded together to form Jane, a clandestine group providing safe abortions in the years before Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 ''The Janes'' is a straightforward, talking-heads documentary from HBO that provides a brief history of the Jane Collective, a clandestine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group working out of Chicago in the late 1960s and early '70s.\par \par \uc2 Roe v. Wade, the 1973 Supreme Court decision that protected a women's right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had not yet been handed down, meaning the procedure was illegal in most states, forcing women with unwanted pregnancies to turn to exploitative \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers (like the Mafia) or resort to dangerous methods to self-induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This situation -- and the can-do spirit of the times, cultivated by the civil rights and women's liberation movements -- sparked the members of Jane into action.\par \par \uc2 [Video: Watch on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .]\par \par \uc2 The documentary, directed by Tia Lessin and Emma Pildes, relies primarily on testimonies from the Jane Collective's women volunteers, tracing their efforts from the beginning -- when the group was merely a referral service -- to their final days contending with law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the Jane Collective provided close to 11,000 abortions by the time Roe v. Wade came into effect, at which point the group ceased its activities. (Though the renewed push for restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws today, and reports of the present Supreme Court's ruling on a case that could overturn Roe, casts a sense of bleak uncertainty over the film's otherwise triumphant conclusion.)\par \par \uc2 Cookie-cutter though it is, ''The Janes'' does have something going for it: its interview subjects, the former Janes, who all speak about their beliefs and shared past with striking clarity. They remind us that their work -- their commitment to ensuring the safety and well-being of other women -- was not really all that radical, but a measured, intelligent response to the inadequacies of a system that refused to fend for its own.\par \par \uc2 The Janes\par \par \uc2 Not rated. Running time: 1 hour 41 minutes. Watch on HBO platforms.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Jane Collective, an activist group that helped provide safe \uc2  in the years before Roe v. Wade. (PHOTOGRAPH BY HBO FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220610ei6a0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
